			},
			"date": "2025-06-05T20:07:06.151Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://mastodon.social/@loucyx\" class=\"u-url mention\">@<span>loucyx</span></a></span> thanks for testing! fair point about overscroll, I don’t think there is an `overscroll-behavior` value that makes sense for the component to add though — this seems more like an app-level option</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
		{
			"id": "114632571355869542",
			"parentId": "114632558257858723",
			"url": "https://mastodon.social/@loucyx/114632571278661769",
			"author": {
				"name": "Lou Cyx",
				"url": "https://mastodon.social/@loucyx",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/111/269/831/992/438/037/original/7daf75da2c4f3371.png"
			},
			"date": "2025-06-05T20:10:24.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> yup. That's why I pointed it out as \"odd\", mainly because I would expect the line numbers to always be aligned with the lines. Those two things makes it feel \"disconnected\", but I'm guessing that's because the component is non-intrusive, so it adds the line numbers \"next to\" the lines, not \"into\" the lines.</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
